{:edb/db-before-t 2673 :edb/db-after-t 2674 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535986 50 #inst "2026-10-09T12:18:40.251Z" 13194139535986 true] [17592186179478 1100 "Calculate $\\nabla\\times(3\\mathbf{F} + \\mathbf{G})$ at the point $(-1,1,0)$ for the vector fields $\\mathbf F$ and $\\mathbf G$, where\n\n$\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z) = 3x\\,\\mathbf{i} + y^2z\\,\\mathbf{j} + 2\\,\\mathbf{k}, \\quad (\\nabla\\times\\mathbf{G})(x,y,z) = 3y^2\\,\\mathbf{i} + 4z\\,\\mathbf{j} + \\mathbf{k}$." 13194139535986 false] [17592186179478 1100 "Calculate $\\nabla\\times(3\\mathbf{F} + \\mathbf{G})$ at the point $(-1,1,0)$ for the vector fields $\\mathbf F$ and $\\mathbf G,$ where\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z) = 3x\\,\\mathbf{i} + y^2z\\,\\mathbf{j} + 2\\,\\mathbf{k}, \\quad (\\nabla\\times\\mathbf{G})(x,y,z) = 3y^2\\,\\mathbf{i} + 4z\\,\\mathbf{j} + \\mathbf{k}.\n$$" 13194139535986 true] [17592186179478 1145 "If $\\mathbf F$ and $\\mathbf G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $\\nabla \\times (k \\mathbf F) = k \\nabla \\times \\mathbf F$\n\n- $\\nabla \\times (\\mathbf F + \\mathbf G) = \\nabla \\times \\mathbf F + \\nabla \\times \\mathbf G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (3F+G) & =∇\\times (3F)+∇\\times G \\\\  & =3∇\\times F+∇\\times G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $\\nabla \\times \\mathbf{F}.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ 3x & {y}^{2}z & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({y}^{2}z)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(3x)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}z)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3x)]k \\\\  & =(0-{y}^{2})i-(0-0)j+(0-0)k \\\\  & =-{y}^{2}\\,i.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (3F+G) & =3∇\\times F+∇\\times G \\\\  & =3[-{y}^{2}\\,i]+[3{y}^{2}\\,i+4z\\,j+k] \\\\  & =-3{y}^{2}\\,i+3{y}^{2}\\,i+4z\\,j+k \\\\  & =(3{y}^{2}-3{y}^{2})\\,i+4z\\,j+k \\\\  & =4z\\,j+k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(-1,1,0),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\times (F-G))(-1,1,0) & =4(0)\\,j+k=k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535986 true] [17592186179478 1145 "If $\\mathbf F$ and $\\mathbf G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $\\nabla \\times (k \\mathbf F) = k \\nabla \\times \\mathbf F$\n- $\\nabla \\times (\\mathbf F + \\mathbf G) = \\nabla \\times \\mathbf F + \\nabla \\times \\mathbf G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∇ \\cdot (3F + G) &= ∇ \\cdot (3F) + ∇ \\cdot G \\\\\n&= 3∇ \\cdot F + ∇ \\cdot G\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $\\nabla \\times \\mathbf{F}$. In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∇ \\cdot F &= \\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ 3x & y^{2}z & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= [\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2) - \\frac{∂}{∂z}(y^{2}z)]i - [\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2) - \\frac{∂}{∂z}(3x)]j + [\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y^{2}z) - \\frac{∂}{∂y}(3x)]k \\\\\n&= (0 - y^{2})i - (0 - 0)j + (0 - 0)k \\\\\n&=-y^{2}i\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∇ \\cdot (3F + G) &= 3∇ \\cdot F + ∇ \\cdot G \\\\\n&= 3[- y^{2}i] + [3y^{2}i + 4zj + k] \\\\\n&=-3y^{2}i + 3y^{2}i + 4zj + k \\\\\n&= (3y^{2} - 3y^{2})i + 4zj + k \\\\\n&= 4zj + k\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(-1,1,0)$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(∇ \\cdot (F - G))(-1, 1, 0) &= 4(0)j + k = k\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535986 false] [17592186179480 1100 "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y,z) =  \\langle 0, y-z, x-y\\rangle$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z) = x+y.$ Given that\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\times \\mathbf F = \\langle 0,\\,-1,\\,0\\rangle, \n\\quad\n\\nabla f = \\langle 1,\\, 1,\\, 0\\rangle,\n$$\n\ncalculate $\\nabla\\times(f\\,\\mathbf F)$ at the point $(-1,1,3).$" 13194139535986 true] [17592186179480 1100 "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y,z) = \\langle 0, y-z, x-y\\rangle$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z) = x+y$. Given that\n$\\nabla\\times \\mathbf F = \\langle 0,\\,-1,\\,0\\rangle, \\quad \\nabla f = \\langle 1,\\, 1,\\, 0\\rangle$,\ncalculate $\\nabla\\times(f\\,\\mathbf F)$ at the point $(-1,1,3)$." 13194139535986 false] [17592186179480 1145 "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\times(f\\,\\mathbf F) = f \\nabla \\times \\mathbf {F}+   \\nabla f \\times \\mathbf F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $\\nabla f \\times \\mathbf F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & y-z & x-y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[1\\cdot (x-y)-0\\cdot (y-z)]\\,i-[1\\cdot (x-y)-0\\cdot (0)]\\,j+[1\\cdot (y-z)-1\\cdot (0)]\\,k \\\\  & =(x-y)\\,i+(y-x)\\,j+(y-z)\\,k \\\\  & =⟨x-y,\\,y-x,\\,y-z⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =(x+y)⟨0,-1,0⟩+⟨x-y,\\,y-x,\\,y-z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-(x+y),0⟩+⟨x-y,\\,y-x,\\,y-z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨x-y,\\,-2x,\\,y-z⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(-1,1,3) & =⟨(-1)-1,\\,-2(-1),\\,1-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2,\\,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535986 true] [17592186179480 1145 "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\times(f\\,\\mathbf F) = f \\nabla \\times \\mathbf {F}+ \\nabla f \\times \\mathbf F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $\\nabla f \\times \\mathbf F$. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∇f \\cdot F &= \\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & y - z & x - y\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= [1 \\cdot (x - y) - 0 \\cdot (y - z)]i - [1 \\cdot (x - y) - 0 \\cdot (0)]j + [1 \\cdot (y - z) - 1 \\cdot (0)]k \\\\\n&= (x - y)i + (y - x)j + (y - z)k \\\\\n&= ⟨x - y, y - x, y - z⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∇ \\cdot (fF) &= f∇ \\cdot F + ∇f \\cdot F \\\\\n&= (x + y)⟨0,-1, 0⟩ + ⟨x - y, y - x, y - z⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨0, - (x + y), 0⟩ + ⟨x - y, y - x, y - z⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨x - y,-2x, y - z⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∇ \\cdot (fF)(-1, 1, 3) &= ⟨(-1) - 1,-2(-1), 1 - 3⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 2, 2,-2⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535986 false] [17592186179619 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378270 13194139535986 true] [17592186179619 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378277 13194139535986 true] [17592186179619 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378305 13194139535986 true] [17592186179619 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378312 13194139535986 true] [17592186179619 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378319 13194139535986 true] [17592186179621 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378284 13194139535986 true] [17592186179621 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378291 13194139535986 true] [17592186179621 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378298 13194139535986 true] [17592186179621 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378326 13194139535986 true] [17592186179621 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378333 13194139535986 true] [17592186378270 1017 #edb/ref 17592186378271 13194139535986 true] [17592186378270 1089 "q-105792" 13194139535986 true] [17592186378270 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535986 true] [17592186378270 1100 "Calculate $∇\\times (2F-G)$ at the point $(0,-1,2)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)={e}^{x}\\,i+yz\\,j,\\,(∇\\times G)(x,y,z)=z\\,i+(x+2y)\\,k.\n$$" 13194139535986 true] [17592186378270 1113 #uuid "a1665578-dbd9-50ec-867b-48ff886a6d85" 13194139535986 true] [17592186378270 1145 "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (2F-G) & =∇\\times (2F)+∇\\times (-G) \\\\  & =2∇\\times F-∇\\times G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ {e}^{x} & yz & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(0)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(yz)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(0)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({e}^{x})]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(yz)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x})]k \\\\  & =(0-y)i-(0-0)j+(0-0)k \\\\  & =-y\\,i.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (2F-G) & =2∇\\times F-∇\\times G \\\\  & =2[-y\\,i]-[z\\,i+(x+2y)\\,k] \\\\  & =-2y\\,i-z\\,i-(x+2y)\\,k \\\\  & =-(2y+z)\\,i-(x+2y)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(0,-1,2),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\times (2F-G))(0,-1,2) & =-(2(-1)+2)\\,i-(0+2(-1))\\,k \\\\  & =-(-2+2)\\,i-(0-2)\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535986 true] [17592186378271 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378272 13194139535986 true] [17592186378271 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378273 13194139535986 true] [17592186378271 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378274 13194139535986 true] [17592186378271 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378275 13194139535986 true] [17592186378271 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378276 13194139535986 true] [17592186378271 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535986 true] [17592186378271 1041 "selection" 13194139535986 true] [17592186378271 1104 #edb/ref 17592186378276 13194139535986 true] [17592186378271 1110 #uuid "e9001483-ab22-5284-bda2-cad4963b5d32" 13194139535986 true] [17592186378272 1034 "-2\\,i+j" 13194139535986 true] [17592186378272 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535986 true] [17592186378272 1111 #uuid "ced3deef-3369-5c92-a6fd-58af86179357" 13194139535986 true] [17592186378273 1034 "-j+2\\,k" 13194139535986 true] [17592186378273 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535986 true] [17592186378273 1111 #uuid "13f27617-a400-5fd7-b620-5fa97930df42" 13194139535986 true] [17592186378274 1034 "3\\,i" 13194139535986 true] [17592186378274 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535986 true] [17592186378274 1111 #uuid "700756f4-8079-5c3a-954a-c8f8d7280d2d" 13194139535986 true] [17592186378275 1034 "-k" 13194139535986 true] [17592186378275 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535986 true] [17592186378275 1111 #uuid "e68e5919-ec7e-5c94-a7bd-0338054e031b" 13194139535986 true] [17592186378276 1034 "2\\,k" 13194139535986 true] [17592186378276 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535986 true] [17592186378276 1111 #uuid "8819badf-2126-561b-b89a-c0fe25315da4" 13194139535986 true] [17592186378277 1017 #edb/ref 17592186378278 13194139535986 true] [17592186378277 1089 "q-105799" 13194139535986 true] [17592186378277 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535986 true] [17592186378277 1100 "Calculate $∇\\times (F+3G)$ at the point $(0,1,-2)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)={y}^{2}\\,i+z\\,j+{x}^{2}\\,k,\\,(∇\\times G)(x,y,z)=-3{x}^{2}\\,j-k.\n$$" 13194139535986 true] [17592186378277 1113 #uuid "39f7b901-580a-5a32-ab40-fb1a6dc62a95" 13194139535986 true] [17592186378277 1145 "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F+3G) & =∇\\times F+∇\\times (3G) \\\\  & =∇\\times F+3∇\\times G\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ {y}^{2} & z & {x}^{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(z)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({y}^{2})]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(z)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2})]k \\\\  & =(0-1)i-(2x-0)j+(0-2y)k \\\\  & =-i-2x\\,j-2y\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F+3G) & =∇\\times F+3∇\\times G \\\\  & =-i-2x\\,j-2y\\,k+3[-3{x}^{2}\\,j-k] \\\\  & =-i-2x\\,j-2y\\,k-9{x}^{2}\\,j-3k \\\\  & =-i-(9{x}^{2}+2x)\\,j-(2y+3)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(0,1,-2),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\times (F+3G))(0,1,-2) & =-i-(9(0)^{2}+2(0))\\,j-(2(1)+3)\\,k \\\\  & =-i-5\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535986 true] [17592186378278 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378279 13194139535986 true] 