$ at the point $(\\pi ,1,0).$" 13194139535986 true] [17592186378284 1113 #uuid "029ad381-66bf-5214-8d8c-c8e093cae3d1" 13194139535986 true] [17592186378284 1145 "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)=f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2z \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+z) & y & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[0(0)-2z(y)]i-[0(0)-2z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+z)]j+[0(y)-0\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+z)]k \\\\  & =-2yz\\,i+2z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+z)j+0\\,k \\\\  & =⟨-2yz,2z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+z),0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =(1+{z}^{2})⟨0,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+z),0⟩+⟨-2yz,2z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+z),0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,(1+{z}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+z),0⟩+⟨-2yz,2z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+z),0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2yz,(1+{z}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+z)+2z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+z),0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(\\pi ,1,0) & =⟨-2(1)(0),(1+(0)^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi +0)+2(0)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi +0),0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535986 true] [17592186378285 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378286 13194139535986 true] [17592186378285 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378287 13194139535986 true] [17592186378285 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378288 13194139535986 true] [17592186378285 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378289 13194139535986 true] [17592186378285 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378290 13194139535986 true] [17592186378285 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535986 true] [17592186378285 1041 "selection" 13194139535986 true] [17592186378285 1104 #edb/ref 17592186378289 13194139535986 true] [17592186378285 1110 #uuid "c2453c30-2ebc-5720-8567-5235873a1248" 13194139535986 true] [17592186378286 1034 "⟨1,0,0⟩" 13194139535986 true] [17592186378286 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535986 true] [17592186378286 1111 #uuid "2c4d57e2-d89e-546a-8c45-02503